<h2>what we covered</h2>
<table class="recap">
  <tr><td>instructions</td><td>32 registers, ~40 instructions, every one 4 bytes</td></tr>
  <tr><td>c → asm</td><td>variables become registers, <code>if</code> and loops become branches</td></tr>
  <tr><td>call / stack</td><td>call = write ra + jump, ret = jump to ra. sp moves down per call so ra survives</td></tr>
  <tr><td>execution</td><td>pipelined, out of order, all "as if" in order</td></tr>
  <tr><td>caches</td><td>64-byte lines. walk memory in order</td></tr>
</table>
